PRSENSE(1)
PRSENSE — AI-powered, self-hosted code review engine

⸻

NAME
prsense — AI-assisted pull request and repository review engine

⸻

SYNOPSIS
prsense [command] [options] [target]

prsense-daemon

⸻

DESCRIPTION

PRSense is an open-source AI-powered code review engine that surfaces high-confidence review signals from code changes.

It is delivery-agnostic. The same review engine can run:

• As an interactive CLI
• As a long-lived HTTP daemon
• Behind webhooks
• Inside CI pipelines

PRSense focuses on structured review signals rather than autonomous modification. It prioritizes:

• Risk detection
• Change comprehension
• Explicit reasoning
• Deterministic configuration
• Self-hosted infrastructure

PRSense operates on diffs and optionally surrounding repository context using retrieval-augmented generation (RAG). Output is validated, normalized, deduplicated, and filtered by confidence before being emitted.

The CLI and daemon are delivery surfaces over the same core review engine.

⸻

COMMANDS

review      Review a code change and emit structured review signals
index       Index a repository for contextual retrieval (RAG)
doctor      Diagnose PRSense installation and runtime environment
setup       Perform setup readiness checks
daemon      Manage daemon lifecycle (if installed)
help        Show help for a command

⸻

COMMAND: review

NAME
prsense review — review a code change

SYNOPSIS
prsense review [target] [options]

DESCRIPTION

Reviews a code change and produces structured ReviewSignal objects.

The review process:
	1.	Computes a diff
	2.	Retrieves relevant repository context (if indexed)
	3.	Constructs a structured review prompt
	4.	Invokes the configured LLM provider
	5.	Validates and normalizes output
	6.	Filters by confidence threshold
	7.	Deduplicates signals

If no index exists, review falls back to diff-only mode.

TARGETS

.
Current repository (default)

<path>  
    Path to a local repository


https://github.com/…/pull/
GitHub Pull Request

https://gitlab.com/…/-/merge_requests/
GitLab Merge Request

OPTIONS

–base-branch 
Override base branch for diff comparison.

–format <text|json>
Output format (default: text).

–no-context
Disable contextual retrieval (diff-only review).

EXAMPLES

prsense review .
prsense review –base-branch origin/main
prsense review https://github.com/org/repo/pull/42

⸻

COMMAND: index

NAME
prsense index — index repository for contextual review

SYNOPSIS
prsense index [target] [options]

DESCRIPTION

Indexes a repository for retrieval-augmented review (RAG).

Indexing:

• Scans repository files
• Chunks content deterministically
• Generates embeddings
• Stores vectors in PostgreSQL with pgvector
• Tracks repository fingerprint metadata

The process is idempotent and safe to run repeatedly.

Re-indexing is triggered when:

• Commit SHA changes
• Embedding provider changes
• Embedding model changes
• Embedding dimension changes
• Chunking strategy changes
• PRSense version changes

TARGETS

.
Current repository (default)

<path>  
    Path to local repository


https://github.com/org/repo
https://gitlab.com/group/project

OPTIONS

–force
Rebuild index even if up-to-date.

–dry-run
Evaluate index state without writing.

–stats
Print indexing statistics.

–chunk-size 
Override chunk size in characters.

NOTES

Indexing requires:

• PostgreSQL
• pgvector extension
• Valid embedding provider

Embedding dimension must match database schema.

EXAMPLES

prsense index .
prsense index . –force
prsense index https://github.com/org/repo

