COMMAND: doctor

NAME
prsense doctor — diagnose environment and configuration

SYNOPSIS
prsense doctor

DESCRIPTION

Performs structured diagnostic checks:

• Configuration validation
• Credential validation
• Database connectivity
• pgvector availability
• LLM provider configuration
• Repository state

Each check emits structured, actionable results.

EXAMPLES

prsense doctor

⸻

COMMAND: setup

NAME
prsense setup — perform setup readiness checks

SYNOPSIS
prsense setup

DESCRIPTION

Validates first-time setup requirements and readiness.

Focuses on environment and infrastructure availability.
Does not automatically provision services unless explicitly configured.

EXAMPLES

prsense setup

⸻

DAEMON

NAME
prsense-daemon — run PRSense as a long-lived HTTP service

SYNOPSIS
prsense-daemon

DESCRIPTION

Starts the PRSense HTTP daemon.

The daemon exposes endpoints for:

• Review job creation
• Index job creation
• Webhook-triggered reviews
• Health and readiness checks

DEFAULT LISTEN ADDRESS

http://localhost:3000

ENDPOINTS

GET /health
Liveness probe

GET /ready
Readiness probe

POST /jobs/review
Trigger review job

POST /jobs/index
Trigger indexing job

POST /webhooks/github
GitHub pull_request webhook endpoint

POST /webhooks/gitlab
GitLab merge_request webhook endpoint

Webhooks require corresponding webhook secrets configured via environment variables.

⸻

CONFIGURATION

PRSense separates:
	1.	Review behavior configuration (repository-level)
	2.	Runtime configuration and credentials (environment)

USER CONFIGURATION

A file named prsense.yml may be placed at repository root.

Example:

llm:
provider: ollama
model: qwen2.5-coder
temperature: 0.1

embeddings:
provider: ollama
model: nomic-embed-text

review:
confidenceThreshold: 0.6
maxSignals: 10

context:
maxChunks: 5

git:
baseBranch: main

delivery:
	•	github
	•	gitlab

If absent, sensible defaults are applied.

ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES

Environment variables configure infrastructure and credentials.

Common variables:

PRSENSE_DATABASE_URL
PRSENSE_OPENAI_API_KEY
PRSENSE_GEMINI_API_KEY
PRSENSE_CLAUDE_API_KEY
PRSENSE_GITHUB_TOKEN
PRSENSE_GITHUB_APP_ID
PRSENSE_GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY
PRSENSE_GITHUB_INSTALLATION_ID
PRSENSE_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET
PRSENSE_GITLAB_TOKEN
PRSENSE_GITLAB_WEBHOOK_SECRET
PRSENSE_SLACK_BOT_TOKEN
PRSENSE_OLLAMA_HOST
PRSENSE_LOG_LEVEL

Environment variables are validated before workflows execute.

⸻

EXIT STATUS

0   Successful execution
1   Invalid configuration or usage
2   Runtime failure

⸻

FILES

prsense.yml
Repository-local configuration.

~/.config/prsense/
Optional user-level configuration.

~/.local/state/prsense/
Runtime state directory (daemon PID, logs).

⸻

DESIGN PRINCIPLES

PRSense is intentionally:

• Delivery-agnostic
• Self-hosted
• Retrieval-augmented
• Deterministic
• Structured in output
• Explicit in configuration
• Focused on high-signal review

It prioritizes signal quality over verbosity.

